# Root .dockerignore for every image built from the repo-root context
# (apps/portal-api, apps/portal-web, tools/pointcloud-worker). The
# per-app .dockerignore files are inert for those builds: Docker only
# reads the .dockerignore that sits next to the build context root,
# and docker-compose.prod.yml sets `context: ..` (the repo root).
#
# Patterns here are context-root-relative. A pattern without a
# leading **/ only matches at the repo root; keep it that way for the
# scratch-file patterns below so legitimate source under apps/ and
# packages/ (for example apps/portal-web/public/sw.js) is never
# excluded. The Dockerfiles COPY: package.json, pnpm-lock.yaml,
# pnpm-workspace.yaml, turbo.json, tsconfig.base.json, packages/,
# apps/ (including apps/portal-web/content and public), and
# tools/pointcloud-worker/runner.py. Nothing below touches those.

# Heavy build state. All of it is regenerated inside the build.
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/dist
**/.turbo
**/__pycache__
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Version control and editor state.
.git
.obsidian
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db

# Secrets and materialized secret-bearing files. The builds never
# COPY infra/, but keeping these out of the context is defense in
# depth against a future COPY widening.
infra/.env.prod*
infra/keycloak/import

# Logs anywhere in the tree (** matches zero or more directories, so
# this covers root-level logs too).
**/*.log

# Local-only scratch directories.
local_*

# Repo-root scratch files (commit-message drafts, typecheck capture
# files, PowerShell helpers, test uploads). Root-anchored on purpose:
# these patterns must not reach into apps/ or packages/.
*.cmd
*.ps1
*.txt
*.js
*.zip
*.geojson

# Backup archives if BACKUP_DIR was ever pointed inside the repo.
backups
